# __APP_NAME__

__PURPOSE__

This is the Unity Sandbox & Gateway (Minimal) template. It is intentionally
headless — there is no web surface — and includes only the three Minimal
Building Blocks from the [Sandbox & Gateway pattern](../../docs/sandbox-gateway-pattern.md):

- an agent loop reachable over HTTP (`POST /invoke`), with its prompt in
  `src/agent/prompts/system.md`;
- an ACA Sandbox tool boundary at `src/sandbox/tool/` that receives only the
  minimum fields it needs and returns only derived, non-identifying results —
  never the raw input back to the caller;
- an AI Gateway configuration seam for every model call the agent makes.

The template does not invent a domain tool. `src/sandbox/tool/main.py`
illustrates the PII boundary generically (it reads one JSON object from
stdin and returns only aggregate statistics); replace its logic with your own
sandboxed computation without changing the boundary shape.

## Run

```bash
./scripts/dev-start.sh
```

Smoke-test it:

```bash
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8088/invoke \
  -H "content-type: application/json" \
  -d '{"message": "Summarize these three numbers: 10, 20, 30"}'
```

Stop everything with:

```bash
./scripts/dev-stop.sh
```

The startup script uses the Microsoft Python package mirror and starts only
the local agent process. The sandbox tool runs per-invocation as a
subprocess, matching the ACA Sandbox pattern (created fresh, receives one
request, returns one bounded verdict, then exits) rather than running as a
standalone server.
